From: mscharged-port
Subject: Rollback: a replay builds no drawing either
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A rollback replays whole frames and draws nothing (tweak patch 0042): the
models a replayed frame attaches go nowhere (GLView::AttachModel). Building
them still ran, and the profile of a replayed Game Render was 60% the
characters' pose blend (DrawableCharacter::Blend, BuildNodeMatrices), then
the indicators' and meters' polygons (glBuildPoly2Model) and the crowd
impostors' views; a replayed Front End spent 85% walking the scenes'
timelines to attach them (FESceneManager::RenderActiveScenes).

During a replay (mscharged_rollback_resimulating) the 2D polygons and quads
are not built (glPoly2::Attach, glAttachPoly2, glAttachQuad3 say they
attached), the blended characters keep their last drawing's pose (their
positions, heights and facing still blend: the cameras, the ball and the
effects read those), unless an effect that follows the character's joints
read the pose since its last blend (EmissionController::SetPoseAccumulator
marks it in the pose's padding: Waluigi's wall, emitted from a pose a
frame or two old, left gaps where a replay ran), the crowd impostors are left
alone, the front end's scenes are updated but not rendered, the particles
are updated but their quads, models and field lights are not built
(ParticleUpdateTask), and the object blur's trails keep their points but
build no mesh (BlurManager::Update). What those compute is read by the
drawing alone, which the next frame does again.

